Here are the formulas, conversion tables, and an easy way to calculate your grade to a percentage. 

If you want a quick answer, **just reply with your grade (e.g., "17 out of 23" or "B+") and I will calculate it for you instantly!**

Otherwise, you can use the guides below:

---

### 1. Points / Fraction to Percentage (e.g., 45 out of 50)
This is the most common way to calculate a grade.
* **Formula:** $(\text{Points Earned} \div \text{Total Points}) \times 100 = \text{Percentage}$
* **Example:** If you got **37** out of **40** on a test:
  $$37 \div 40 = 0.925$$
  $$0.925 \times 100 = 92.5\%$$

---

### 2. Letter Grade to Percentage Table
This table shows the standard US high school and college grade conversions:

| Letter Grade | Percentage Range | Midpoint / Equivalent |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A+** | 97% – 100% | 98.5% |
| **A** | 93% – 96% | 94.5% |
| **A-** | 90% – 92% | 91.0% |
| **B+** | 87% – 89% | 88.0% |
| **B** | 83% – 86% | 84.5% |
| **B-** | 80% – 82% | 81.0% |
| **C+** | 77% – 79% | 78.0% |
| **C** | 73% – 76% | 74.5% |
| **C-** | 70% – 72% | 71.0% |
| **D+** | 67% – 69% | 68.0% |
| **D** | 65% – 66% | 65.5% |
| **F** | Below 65% | — |

---

### 3. GPA to Percentage (4.0 Scale)
Because schools convert GPAs to percentages differently, these are standard approximations:

* **3.9 – 4.0** $\approx$ 95% – 100%
* **3.7 – 3.8** $\approx$ 90% – 94%
* **3.3 – 3.6** $\approx$ 87% – 89%
* **3.0 – 3.2** $\approx$ 83% – 86%
* **2.7 – 2.9** $\approx$ 80% – 82%
* **2.3 – 2.6** $\approx$ 77% – 79%
* **2.0 – 2.2** $\approx$ 73% – 76%
* **1.0 – 1.9** $\approx$ 65% – 72%

---

### Want your own interactive web calculator?
You can copy the code below, paste it into a blank text file, save it as `calculator.html`, and double-click to open it in any web browser. It works offline and converts points, letter grades, and GPA to percentages!

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Grade to Percentage Calculator</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 400px; margin: 50px auto; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); }
        h2 { text-align: center; }
        label { display: block; margin-top: 10px; }
        input, select, button { width: 100%; padding: 8px; margin-top: 5px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        button { background-color: #007BFF; color: white; border: none; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 15px; }
        button:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }
        #result { margin-top: 20px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; font-size: 18px; color: #333; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>Grade Calculator</h2>
    <label for="calcType">Choose Conversion Type:</label>
    <select id="calcType" onchange="toggleInputs()">
        <option value="points">Points Earned / Total Points</option>
        <option value="letter">Letter Grade to %</option>
        <option value="gpa">GPA to %</option>
    </select>

    <div id="pointsDiv">
        <label for="earned">Points Earned:</label>
        <input type="number" id="earned" placeholder="e.g. 45" step="any">
        <label for="total">Total Points:</label>
        <input type="number" id="total" placeholder="e.g. 50" step="any">
    </div>

    <div id="letterDiv" style="display:none;">
        <label for="letter">Select Letter Grade:</label>
        <select id="letter">
            <option value="98">A+ (97-100%)</option>
            <option value="95">A (93-96%)</option>
            <option value="91">A- (90-92%)</option>
            <option value="88">B+ (87-89%)</option>
            <option value="85">B (83-86%)</option>
            <option value="81">B- (80-82%)</option>
            <option value="78">C+ (77-79%)</option>
            <option value="75">C (73-76%)</option>
            <option value="71">C- (70-72%)</option>
            <option value="68">D+ (67-69%)</option>
            <option value="65">D (63-66%)</option>
            <option value="61">D- (60-62%)</option>
            <option value="50">F (Below 60%)</option>
        </select>
    </div>

    <div id="gpaDiv" style="display:none;">
        <label for="gpa">Enter GPA (out of 4.0):</label>
        <input type="number" id="gpa" placeholder="e.g. 3.7" step="0.01" min="0" max="4.0">
    </div>

    <button onclick="calculate()">Calculate</button>
    <div id="result"></div>

    <script>
        function toggleInputs() {
            var type = document.getElementById("calcType").value;
            document.getElementById("pointsDiv").style.display = type === "points" ? "block" : "none";
            document.getElementById("letterDiv").style.display = type === "letter" ? "block" : "none";
            document.getElementById("gpaDiv").style.display = type === "gpa" ? "block" : "none";
            document.getElementById("result").innerText = "";
        }

        function calculate() {
            var type = document.getElementById("calcType").value;
            var resultDiv = document.getElementById("result");

            if (type === "points") {
                var earned = parseFloat(document.getElementById("earned").value);
                var total = parseFloat(document.getElementById("total").value);
                if (isNaN(earned) || isNaN(total) || total === 0) {
                    resultDiv.innerText = "Please enter valid points.";
                    return;
                }
                var pct = (earned / total) * 100;
                resultDiv.innerText = pct.toFixed(2) + "%";
            } else if (type === "letter") {
                var pctVal = document.getElementById("letter").value;
                resultDiv.innerText = "Approx. " + pctVal + "%";
            } else if (type === "gpa") {
                var gpa = parseFloat(document.getElementById("gpa").value);
                if (isNaN(gpa) || gpa < 0 || gpa > 4.0) {
                    resultDiv.innerText = "Please enter a GPA between 0.0 and 4.0.";
                    return;
                }
                var pct;
                if (gpa >= 3.9) pct = "95% - 100%";
                else if (gpa >= 3.7) pct = "90% - 94%";
                else if (gpa >= 3.3) pct = "87% - 89%";
                else if (gpa >= 3.0) pct = "83% - 86%";
                else if (gpa >= 2.7) pct = "80% - 82%";
                else if (gpa >= 2.3) pct = "77% - 79%";
                else if (gpa >= 2.0) pct = "73% - 76%";
                else if (gpa >= 1.7) pct = "70% - 72%";
                else if (gpa >= 1.3) pct = "67% - 69%";
                else if (gpa >= 1.0) pct = "65% - 66%";
                else pct = "Below 65%";

                resultDiv.innerText = "Approx. " + pct;
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

